  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Set a physbone to respond to a collider with \"Is Animated\" enabled, and then make it animate in such a way to try to go through the collider (Quick way to prove it;  Put a physbone on your avatar's arm and a collider in your avatar's body).  It will act like the collider is not there rather than hitting the collider as-intended.\nI don't know if this is intended behaviour, but it was a really useful tool for avatars with unusual body shapes like mine with dynamic bones, where I could maintain a general humanoid range of limb movement without the limbs clipping inside the body constantly.",
